upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about the process of denudation:\n1. Denudation is carried out in four phases: weathering, erosion, transportation and deposition.\n2. Weathering is defined as the gradual disintegration of rocks by atmospheric or weather forces, without any active removal of material by moving agents.\n3. All four phases occur strictly one after another in a fixed sequence across the entire globe at the same time.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect — the text explicitly states that all four phases are taking place SIMULTANEOUSLY in different parts of the world at different rates, depending on relief, rock structure, climate and human interference, not in a fixed global sequence. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements distinguishing weathering from erosion:\n1. Weathering is the gradual disintegration of rocks by atmospheric or weather forces, occurring largely in place.\n2. Erosion is the active wearing away of the Earth's surface by moving agents such as running water, wind, ice and waves.\n3. Transportation refers to the dumping of eroded debris in certain parts of the earth where it may accumulate to form new rocks.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect and describes deposition, not transportation — transportation is the REMOVAL of eroded debris to new positions, while deposition is the actual dumping/accumulation of that debris. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Assertion (A): The Earth's surface shows great diversity of present-day landforms.\nReason (R): This diversity results from the interaction between constructive internal forces (such as orogenesis, folding, faulting and volcanic activity) and destructive external forces (denudation).\nWhich one of the following is correct in respect of the above Assertion (A) and Reason (R)?","o":["Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is NOT the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true"],"a":0,"e":"Both are true and R explains A — the text explicitly attributes landform diversity to the interaction of constructive forces (mountain-building, folding, faulting, volcanism) working simultaneously with destructive denudational forces that wear the surface down."})

