# SECTION 2: CHEMICAL WEATHERING - SOLUTION
# ==================================================================

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about chemical weathering:\n1. It is an extremely slow and gradual decomposition of rocks due to exposure to air and water.\n2. When a soil cover exists over rock, chemical weathering of the underlying rock ceases entirely because the soil acts as a protective barrier.\n3. Rain-water that has absorbed organic acids from soil becomes a stronger weathering agent than pure rain-water acting on bare rock.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 3 only","1 and 2 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 2 is incorrect and reverses the actual relationship — the text states that chemical weathering under a soil cover is usually ENHANCED (not ceased), because the soil absorbs rain-water and keeps the underlying rock in prolonged contact with moisture. Statements 1 and 3 are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about solution as a chemical weathering process:\n1. Rain-water containing dissolved carbon dioxide acts as a weak acid capable of dissolving many minerals.\n2. Solution is the most potent weathering process in limestone regions because rain-water dissolves the calcium carbonate of which limestone is chiefly composed.\n3. Limestone is the only rock type that is subject to solution weathering; all other rock types are entirely immune to it.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect — the text explicitly states that ALL rocks are subject to solution to some extent, though the process is much slower than with limestone; limestone is not uniquely susceptible. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about factors affecting the rate of solution weathering:\n1. Sedimentary rocks often have pore-spaces between grains in which air and water can lodge and attack the rock.\n2. The density of joints or cracks in a rock is crucial to the speed of weathering, as clearly seen in the weathering of granite in Malaysia.\n3. In tropical countries, heavy rainfall and warm climate together slow down chemical reactions, producing shallow regoliths.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect and reverses the actual effect — heavy rainfall and warm climate in tropical countries PROMOTE rapid chemical reactions, producing very DEEP regoliths, not shallow ones. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about core-stones:\n1. Core-stones are pieces of solid rock that have resisted weathering while all surrounding rock has been weathered.\n2. They are more resistant because they have fewer joints or cracks to harbour moisture, making them more slowly weathered by solution processes.\n3. Core-stones typically form in areas with unevenly spaced joints, a phenomenon described as differential weathering.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1, 2 and 3","1 and 2 only","2 and 3 only","1 and 3 only"],"a":0,"e":"All three statements are correct, describing how uneven joint spacing in rocks like granite leads to differential weathering, leaving behind more resistant, less-jointed blocks (core-stones) embedded within more thoroughly weathered surrounding material."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about the influence of climate on weathering:\n1. Warm wet climates promote rapid chemical weathering.\n2. Dry climates inhibit chemical weathering but provide good conditions for physical or mechanical weathering.\n3. Climate has no measurable influence on the rate or type of weathering that occurs in a region.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect and directly contradicts statements 1 and 2 — the text explicitly links climate type to which weathering process dominates: warm and wet climates favour chemical weathering, while dry climates favour mechanical weathering instead. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

# ==================================================================
# SECTION 3: OXIDATION AND ORGANIC ACIDS
